# ops/env.example
#
# Reference for every environment variable the ops/*.sh scripts and
# deploy/*.service units read. Copy the relevant sections into the
# EnvironmentFile paths the units expect (see each .service file), or
# `source` this directly for manual/interactive use. Nothing in here is
# loaded automatically -- it's documentation with real variable names, not
# a file the scripts read implicitly.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- shared: output path
# THE single authoritative variable for where generated outputs live on
# disk. ops/launch_comfyui.sh passes this to ComfyUI via --output-directory
# (overriding ComfyUI's own default of <COMFYUI_DIR>/output), and
# ops/sync_outputs.sh's SYNC_SRC defaults to this same path. Override
# COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR here if you need a different path -- do NOT override
# SYNC_SRC and ComfyUI's output directory independently, or they will drift
# apart again: that drift (launch/ComfyUI side implicitly defaulting to
# /opt/ComfyUI/output, sync side defaulting to /opt/comfy-controller/output)
# is exactly the output-path mismatch this variable fixes.
COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR=/opt/comfy-controller/output
# If the controller side (src/comfy_controller/config.py's comfy_output_dir,
# used to match generated files back to a job_key) needs to agree too --
# it's a separate process with its own env-override mechanism -- set this
# to the SAME path as COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR above:
COMFYCTL_COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR=/opt/comfy-controller/output

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- launch_comfyui.sh
# COMFYUI_COMMIT has no default on purpose -- the script refuses to start
# without it (see ops/launch_comfyui.sh's own comment on why the pin is
# deliberate).
COMFYUI_COMMIT=REPLACE_WITH_PINNED_SHA
COMFYUI_REPO_URL=https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI.git
COMFYUI_DIR=/opt/ComfyUI
# 127.0.0.1, NOT 0.0.0.0: the controller only ever talks to ComfyUI at
# 127.0.0.1:8188, and ComfyUI's /prompt (accepts arbitrary workflows,
# including file read/write via node inputs) and /history (job data) have
# no authentication of their own. A wildcard bind buys this deployment
# nothing and exposes both on whatever public IP this rented box has.
COMFYUI_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Loud, explicit opt-in required for anything wider than loopback (see the
# check at the top of ops/launch_comfyui.sh). Leave at 0 unless you have a
# real reason (e.g. controller and ComfyUI on different hosts) AND have
# locked this down at the firewall/security-group layer first -- see
# docs/runbook.md's firewall section.
COMFYUI_ALLOW_NONLOOPBACK_HOST=0
COMFYUI_PORT=8188
# COMFYUI_PYTHON=/opt/ComfyUI/.venv/bin/python   # auto-detected if unset
COMFYUI_LOG_DIR=/var/log/comfy-controller
GUARD_NODE_TIMEOUT_S=90

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- deadman.sh
DEADMAN_HARD_CEILING_MIN=660
DEADMAN_HEARTBEAT_FILE=/opt/comfy-controller/.comfy_supervisor/heartbeat
DEADMAN_HEARTBEAT_STALE_MIN=20
# How long a MISSING heartbeat file is tolerated as "still starting up"
# (controller boot, ComfyUI model load) rather than treated as a dead
# controller. See ops/deadman.sh's check_heartbeat()/_seconds_since_startup_
# marker() for the exact semantics (anchored to a tmpfs marker under /run,
# so it resets every real reboot).
DEADMAN_STARTUP_GRACE_MIN=15
DEADMAN_LOG_FILE=/var/log/comfy-controller/deadman.log

# The controller side of the SAME heartbeat file above
# (src/comfy_controller/config.py's heartbeat_file, read by
# BatchRunner._maybe_touch_heartbeat) -- set this to the SAME path as
# DEADMAN_HEARTBEAT_FILE, exactly like COMFYCTL_COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR mirrors
# COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR above. Do not let these two drift apart, or layer 2 will
# be watching a file the controller never writes.
COMFYCTL_HEARTBEAT_FILE=/opt/comfy-controller/.comfy_supervisor/heartbeat
# COMFYCTL_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_S=30

# One of: runpod | lambda | vast | none
# "none" still arms layer 1 and still runs local `shutdown -h now` from
# layer 2 -- it just skips the provider API call. Read
# ops/deadman.sh's terminate_instance() comment before trusting "none" for a
# real overnight run: local shutdown is not guaranteed to stop billing on
# every provider.
DEADMAN_PROVIDER=none

# -- only if DEADMAN_PROVIDER=runpod (implemented: DELETE /v1/pods/{id} --
# see runpod_terminate() in ops/deadman.sh)
# RUNPOD_API_KEY=
# RUNPOD_POD_ID=

# -- only if DEADMAN_PROVIDER=lambda (implemented: POST
# /api/v1/instance-operations/terminate -- see lambda_terminate() in ops/deadman.sh)
# LAMBDA_API_KEY=
# LAMBDA_INSTANCE_ID=

# -- only if DEADMAN_PROVIDER=vast -- NOT implemented (left as a labelled
# stub: Vast.ai's current terminate-instance API was not verified against
# its own docs in this pass -- see vast_terminate() in ops/deadman.sh. Using
# DEADMAN_PROVIDER=vast still gets the guaranteed local-shutdown fallback,
# just not a provider-side terminate call.)
# VAST_API_KEY=
# VAST_INSTANCE_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sync_outputs.sh
# rclone | s3
SYNC_BACKEND=rclone
# Defaults to COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR above -- only set this separately if outputs
# really do need to be synced from somewhere other than where ComfyUI
# writes them (uncommon; think twice before doing this).
# SYNC_SRC=/opt/comfy-controller/output
# rclone destination form: "remote:bucket/prefix" (configure the remote
# with `rclone config` -- R2 and S3 both work as rclone remotes)
# s3 destination form:     "s3://bucket/prefix"
SYNC_DEST=REPLACE_WITH_REMOTE_DEST
SYNC_INTERVAL_S=30
# Not /tmp -- world-writable, so any local user could hold this lock and
# stall off-box syncing all night. Under the service user's own state dir.
SYNC_LOCK_FILE=/opt/comfy-controller/.comfy_sync/sync-outputs.lock
SYNC_LOG_FILE=/var/log/comfy-controller/sync-outputs.log
# SYNC_RCLONE_EXTRA_ARGS="--transfers=4"
# SYNC_S3_EXTRA_ARGS=""
